# Design direction

All UI work must support a **premium healthcare growth ecosystem**: a **modern digital marketing agency for medicine**—confident, elegant, conversion-driven, and **physician-friendly**. The site should feel like **Influx Marketing** or **Cardinal Digital Marketing**–class polish: vibrant but controlled, never a tech bunker or cybersecurity product UI.

## Canonical feeling

- **Premium, vibrant, approachable** — aspirational for doctors and practice leaders, not cold engineering.
- **Growth-focused** — outcomes, patient acquisition, revenue clarity; AI/tech framed as a **healthcare growth engine**, not infrastructure fetish.
- **Sophisticated motion** — marketing-agency timing (ease, restraint), not sci-fi HUD loops or gamer UI.

## Palette & surfaces

- **Bases:** dark navy, charcoal, rich blue depths—not harsh pure black or neon-soaked voids.
- **Highlights:** cyan / teal for clarity, links, and “digital health” credibility.
- **Conversion warmth:** warm orange (and existing gold where used for CTAs/highlights)—disciplined, not rainbow.
- **Cards:** clean **glassmorphism** (blur, soft border, subtle shadow)—**premium healthcare SaaS**, not holographic panels.

## What to avoid (legacy themes — do not reintroduce)

The following are **out of scope** for this brand; treat them as bugs if they appear:

- Cyberpunk, hacker bunker, “server room,” excessive **grids**, nodes, holograms, cluttered **dashboard screenshots** as default decoration.
- Bright **sparkles**, white particle fields, checkerboards, overexposed glows, dense sci-fi chrome.
- Cartoon icons, gaming UI chrome, ornamental tech-for-tech’s-sake.

## What to use instead

- **Modern dark gradients** with breathable spacing and one focal accent per section where possible.
- **Proof and authority** — metrics, testimonials, outcomes with strong contrast; human/clinical credibility over abstract infra art.
- **Technology** — suggest intelligence and workflow (subtle mesh, soft gradients, restrained canvas) only when it supports the **growth story**.

## Typography & hierarchy

- Strong heading hierarchy; display sans for impact; eyebrows/labels readable and calm (avoid screaming mono sci-fi unless explicitly requested).
- Scan-friendly for busy clinicians—clear first line, supporting detail second.

## Motion

- Smooth, intentional, professional; supports narrative and CTA clarity.
- Honor **`prefers-reduced-motion`**.
- GSAP / Locomotive / canvas: see `premium-layout-3d-motion.mdc`.

## References (inspiration only—not clones)

- [Influx Marketing](https://www.influxmarketing.com/)
- [Cardinal Digital Marketing](https://www.cardinaldigitalmarketing.com/) (pattern-level inspiration)

Pair with **`influx-inspired-vibrancy.mdc`** for accent discipline and section rhythm.

## Responsive quality

Every section must hold from **320px** through large desktop (`responsive-mobile-first.mdc`). Energy on small screens = contrast + spacing + typography, not hover-only tricks.
